                <person xml:id="RUT02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Rutherford</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Married <persName key="FEN02">Eliza Fenwick</persName>'s daughter, <persName key="FEN04">Eliza Ann Fenwick</persName> in
    Barbados, but came to Britain to develop a career as an actor (his wife having acted in the Barbadoes). He was the son of Thomas Rutherford, who was a protege of Eliza 
    Fenwick's father Peter Jaco (also a Methodist Minister), and Rutherford came to Britain partly so that his career choice would not embarrass his parents.  
    Rutherford had a reputation as succumbing to the vice of his father-in-law, drunkeness.
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">Ann Wedd,<title>The Fate of the Fenwicks</title></bibl>
